11	>Conditional	$Variable.1=1	18
12	Display.Conversation	Bert	It held? Of course it held. Oh, don't look at me like that: I only half thought it would.\Listen. The first king cut the dragon down, and the greater part of it didn't die. It went somewhere: the Shardrealm, where all broken magic goes. The barrier draws on it. It's anchored there, beyond the world.	How do I get there?	13
13	Display.Conversation	Bert	You build a door. Not a little one. Any old shardstone can reach the realm's rim, where it's calm and thin and small things hold. That homestead of yours, if you've one? The Stillwater, the settlers call it. It's a pocket of the rim, held by your anchor. Never wondered why it has no neighbours? But the barrier's anchor is at the core, a storm where all the broken magic pools, and you have to pierce that. Only a great anchor of your own will do it: a Shardgate. The old ring of standing stones on the hill north of this Court was one, once.\Here are my plans. Silver, sapphires, a Remnant's core, and Shards: it drinks them. And it must be steadied: wake the shardstones of Brambleton, eight at the least, so the ring has something to hold to while it drives through. Through the gate, find the anchor and break it with the staff. Something will be guarding it. Something always is.	I'll build it.	14
